# CR - Crunch one file

```text
CR [drive:]file [destination-drive:]
```

## Crunch a file

```text
B0:CR A:REPORT.TXT D:
```

CR writes a CRUNCH stream to D:REPORT.TZT and retains the source. Supply
one exact filename in the current user area. If you omit the
destination, output goes to the logged drive.

## Crunch a topic

```text
B0:CR A:PIP.HLP D:
```

The resulting PIP.HZP can go directly into a help library. To recover
the source text before editing, use [UNCR](UNCR.HLP).
